Yices SMT Solver
=============================================

Copyright (c) 2026, SRI International
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

This applies to the Yices source. This archive also contains GMP and
LibPoly. These are covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License; NOTICES
states which version applies to each. Both carry copyright notices in
individual source files rather than one notice for the project, so NOTICES
reproduces no invented project-level copyright line for either library.
Section 3.5 reproduces the distinct LibPoly source-file notices. A relink kit for
rebuilding against your own versions of those libraries is published as a
separate asset on the release page.

The `darwinNN.N.N` component in an archive filename identifies the build host.
It is not the minimum supported macOS version: every Mach-O object in this
archive has deployment target macOS 11.0.

For Apple Silicon, the `aarch64` component identifies the 64-bit Arm
architecture; every Mach-O object in that archive is `arm64`.

The Apple Silicon archive's four executables and shared library carry ad hoc
linker signatures. Their Intel counterparts are unsigned. Object files inside
lib/libyices.a are unsigned on both architectures. Neither archive is signed
with an Apple Developer ID or notarized.

A browser download may carry macOS quarantine metadata and be subject to
Gatekeeper approval before first use; an ad hoc signature is not notarization.
After verifying the archive checksum, a shell report of `Killed: 9`, exit 137,
or no version output can indicate quarantine rather than a solver failure.
Inspect it with `xattr -lr <extracted-directory>` and, if the archive came from
the expected release, clear it with
`xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine <extracted-directory>` before retrying.


Content
-------

This distribution includes four solvers

  bin/yices       (for the Yices 2 language)
  bin/yices-smt   (for SMT-LIB 1.2)
  bin/yices-smt2  (for SMT-LIB 2.0)
  bin/yices-sat   (sat solver, DIMACS format)

and the Yices libraries and header files

  lib/__DYLIB__
  lib/libyices.a
  lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc
  include/yices.h
  include/yices_types.h
  include/yices_limits.h
  include/yices_exit_codes.h


Examples and documentation are in the examples and doc directories.


The Yices shared library and the binaries other than the sat solver were
linked statically against GMP version __GMP__, copyright Free Software
Foundation (see NOTICES).


pkg-config
----------

The file lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc supports `pkg-config --cflags` and
`pkg-config --modversion` from the unpacked archive. The `--libs` and
`--static --libs` results do not produce a working link from the archive as
shipped. The archive has no unversioned shared-library link, so `-lyices`
selects libyices.a, and the private dependency archives named by Libs.private
are not included in lib/.

The installer creates the unversioned shared-library link and installs
yices.pc in <prefix>/lib/pkgconfig.


Installation
------------

The library's install name is '@rpath/__DYLIB__'. A program that links against
it must supply a run-path, normally with
`-Wl,-rpath,/path/to/yices/lib` at link time, or set `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` at
run time.
This distribution includes a shell script to copy the files into an
installation prefix. For a non-destructive installation, choose a fresh
prefix that you own:

   YICES_PREFIX="$HOME/.local/yices-2.8.0"
   ./install-yices "$YICES_PREFIX"

This copies the binaries, headers, shared library, pkg-config file, and legal
record below that prefix. Add "$YICES_PREFIX/bin" to PATH when you want these
binaries. Library users can set PKG_CONFIG_PATH to
"$YICES_PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig" and must still supply the run-path described
above.

The installer does not copy `lib/libyices.a` or `doc/manual.pdf`. Keep the
extracted distribution when you need the static archive or the manual.

The installer refuses to replace any existing Yices file or link. If you
intentionally want to replace an installation in a shared prefix, review that
prefix first and use the explicit option:

   sudo ./install-yices --replace-existing /usr/local

Try ./install-yices --help for more explanations.



For more information, please visit https://yices.csl.sri.com.
